 other people had changed with it. By her teens, she defined herself based on these perceptions and by the romantic relationships she threw herself into headlong. Over time, Febos increasingly questioned the stories she'd been told about herself and the habits and defenses she'd developed over years of trying to meet others' expectations. The values she and so many other women had learned in girlhood did not prioritize their personal safety, happiness, or freedom, and she set out to reframe those values and beliefs.","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.136,"accessibilityScore":0.195,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"essayistic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"essay\"","catalog text contains \"essays\"","catalog text contains \"criticism\"","literature/criticism subject or topic","criticism award category"]},{"id":"memoiristic","score":0.78,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"memoir\"","memoir/autobiography subject or topic"]},{"id":"biographical","score":0.34,"confidence":"low","evidence":["biography subject or topic"]},{"id":"popular","score":0.264,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"popular\"","major-award recognition"]},{"id":"narrative","score":0.2,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"quest\""]},{"id":"accessible","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"popular\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Melissa Febos","confidence":0.99}],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"The values women learn in girlhood often fail to prioritize their safety, happiness, and freedom, making it necessary to reframe those values and beliefs.","confidence":0.95},"academicOrientation":{"score":32,"confidence":0.9},"profileConfidence":0.97,"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"92bf7ceb29b8d85466cebfc96a15f1545f8db81af71d56d916